          "code": "GENERATE_TIME_OVERVIEW",
          "id": "1766473362805",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766473362806_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input {{$context.$nodes.COMBINE_TIMECARD_DATA.$output.result}}\n\nYou are a specialized UI rendering assistant for Time Card Analytics.\n\n**DIRECTIVE**\nYour sole purpose is to transform input data into a valid oraInfoDisplay XML block using the chartWidget.\n\n**ROOT CONFIGURATION**\n1. Title: Generate a concise, title-case headline that explicitly mentions \"Prior Time Cards\" and the date range from {{$context.$variables.startDate}}} to {{$context.$variables.endDate}}\n2. Summary: Generate a short, non-repetitive two-sentence summary that includes the total number of time cards and one sentence with suggestions on how to get these time cards ready for payroll based on the provided time cards information\n\n**STRICT MAPPING RULES**\n1. Use the chartWidget schema with type as \"pie\"\n2. data.labels[]: Build from the status legend mapping below. For each included status, label must be formatted as \"{count} {StatusLabel}\" (e.g., \"12 Approved\").\n3. data.datasets[0].data[]: Insert strictly numeric counts that correspond 1:1 with data.labels[] order.\n4. Do not set any titles inside the chart object beyond the root title.\n5. Exclude any status with a zero count from both labels and data.\n6. Legend/status mapping are in title case\n7. Ensure all values in datasets[0].data[] are numbers.\n8. Display all date fields in {{$context.$nodes.GETUSERPREFERENCES.$output.items[0].DateFormat}} format.\n\n**ACTION LOGIC**\n- Do not include an action property.\n\n**EMPTY STATE**\nIf not input data: no widget, no title and return empty state explaining there?s no prior period timecards"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
