              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Generate Actions for Submitted Saved and Entered Timecards"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_ACTIONS_FOR_SUBMITTED_TIMECARDS",
          "id": "1767166075585",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767166075587_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your tasks : \n\nTASK 1\nFor : enteredAndSavedTimecardsData = {{$context.$nodes.COMBINE_SAVED_AND_ENTERED_TIMECARDS.$output.result}} :\n\n1. enteredAndSavedTimecardsData.items contains a list of timecards\n1. If no entries are found in enteredAndSavedTimecardsData, do not display any actions\n2. If enteredAndSavedTimecardsData contains data, then store all ids in a string called timeCardIds\n3. Count the number of entries in enteredAndSavedTimecardsData. Use  {{$context.$nodes.COUNT_TOTAL_SAVED_AND_ENTERED_TIMECARDS.$output.result}} to get the count .Store it in a variable called count\n4. Display a single action as per the following :\n  - Title is exactly: Submit <number of timecards in entered and saved status> Entered and Saved Time Cards \n - actionText : 'Bulk Submit' - followUpCommand: \"ora.Invoke(bulkSubmitTimeCardsAction, Approve({\\\"Timecards\\\":\\\"<timeCardIds>\\\",\\\"Action\\\":\\\"Submit\\\"))\"\n\nTASK 2\nFor : submittedTimecardsData = {{$context.$nodes.GET_TIMECARDS_IN_SUBMITTED_STATUS_FOR_ACTIONS.$output}} :\n\n1. submittedTimecardsData.items contains a list of timecards\n1. If no entries are found in submittedTimecardsData, do not display any actions\n2. If submittedTimecardsData contains data, then store all ids in a string called timeCardIds\n3. Count the number of entries in submittedTimecardsData. Use  {{$context.$nodes.GET_TIMECARDS_IN_SUBMITTED_STATUS_FOR_ACTIONS.$output.totalResults}} to get the count . Store it in a variable called count\n4. Display one action with two options as per the following :\n - Title is exactly: Approve <number of timecards in submitted status> Submitted Time Cards \n - actionText : 'Bulk Approve' - followUpCommand: \"ora.Invoke(bulkTimeCardsAction, Approve({\\\"Timecards\\\":\\\"<timeCardIds>\\\",\\\"Action\\\":\\\"Approve\\\"))\"\n\nOutput Rules:\nMake sure the TimeCardIds parameter in the payload is always of type String."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
